
Methos :


What is a Method in Java?
A method is a block of code that performs a specific task.


Why Use Methods?
✅ Reusability – Write once, use many times
✅ Easy to read and manage
✅ Reduces code duplication

returnType methodName(parameters) {
    // method body
}



Example 1: A simple method with no parameters and no return
java
Copy
Edit
public static void greet() {
    System.out.println("Hello, Shaik ji!");
}


 How to call this method?
java
Copy
Edit
public static void main(String[] args) {
    greet();  // method call
}

Example 2: Method with parameters (but no return)
java
Copy
Edit
public static void welcomeUser(String name) {
    System.out.println("Welcome, " + name);
}

welcomeUser("Sumiyah");


Example 3: Method with return type
java
Copy
Edit
public static int add(int a, int b) {
    return a + b;
}

int result = add(5, 3);
System.out.println("Result: " + result);


